    fix(plugin): H3-GAP-092 - verify accepts positional NAME
    
    Addresses H3-GAP-092
    
    `hermes-h3 verify [NAME]` has accepted an optional positional NAME since
    DOGFOOD-11 (NAME aliases --harness and wins over it), but the `h3/` Core
    plugin mirror only declared --harness/-H for verify.  Mirror drift again:
    `hermes h3 verify myharness` died in argparse with exit 2 and
    `hermes h3: error: unrecognized arguments: myharness` while the click
    command's own help advertised `[NAME]` — reproduced against the pre-change
    source (SystemExit 2, exit code 2).
    
    Fix mirrors the already-landed install precedent (DF-H3-3) exactly:
    `_POSITIONALS["verify"]` gains the optional `name` entry and the verify
    subparser declares it with `nargs="?"`, `default=None`, so an unset NAME is
    omitted from the rebuilt argv (click then resolves default_harness itself).
    No `_OPTIONS`/`_DEFAULTS` entry is needed — "name" is a positional, and its
    `<field>_opt` fallback only applies when a `--<field>` alias exists, which
    verify does not have in click.
    
    Precedence is NOT re-implemented: when both NAME and --harness are supplied
    the mirror forwards both tokens and click applies its own rule (positional
    NAME wins), so plugin and standalone surfaces cannot drift on this again.
    `verify` with no NAME and `verify --harness NAME` rebuild to byte-identical
    argvs to before.
    
    Tests (tests/test_h3_plugin.py, real plugin reconstruction + real click
    group, no hand-written argvs):
    - verify myharness parses and rebuilds to ["verify", "myharness"];
    - all three forms rebuild faithfully (positional / bare / --harness);
    - positional NAME reaches the same click path as `hermes-h3 verify NAME` —
      asserted on click OUTPUT equality between the plugin-reconstructed
      invocation and the direct one (harness/endpoint resolved via a two-harness
      config with H3Client stubbed);
    - no-NAME still resolves default_harness, --harness still works, and
      NAME + --harness together resolves to NAME.
    
    RED proof before commit: with h3/__init__.py temporarily restored from the
    pre-change copy (md5 af883213a111fe9096054c0c16ee9353, HEAD 02f8f65),
    4 of the new tests fail with the production error verbatim
    (`hermes h3: error: unrecognized arguments: myharness` / `: alpha`,
    SystemExit: 2) while the unchanged-behaviour tests pass — then the
    implementation was restored and all pass.
    
    Verification at this tree: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` → 381 passed;
    `.venv/bin/python -m ruff check src tests h3` → All checks passed;
    `.venv/bin/python -m ruff format --check h3/__init__.py tests/test_h3_plugin.py`
    → 2 files already formatted.  Diff is limited to h3/__init__.py (+8) and
    tests/test_h3_plugin.py (+195); no CLI, docs, or board changes.
    
